.TH "libnvmf_tid_from_fields" 9 "libnvmf_tid_from_fields" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_tid_from_fields \- Allocate a TID from individual field strings.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_tid_from_fields
.BI "(const char *transport "  ","
.BI "const char *traddr "  ","
.BI "const char *trsvcid "  ","
.BI "const char *subsysnqn "  ","
.BI "const char *host_traddr "  ","
.BI "const char *host_iface "  ","
.BI "const char *hostnqn "  ","
.BI "const char *hostid "  ","
.BI "struct libnvmf_tid **out "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "transport" 12
Transport type (e.g. "tcp", "rdma", "fc").
.IP "traddr" 12
Transport address.
.IP "trsvcid" 12
Transport service ID (e.g. "8009").
.IP "subsysnqn" 12
Subsystem NQN.
.IP "host_traddr" 12
Host transport address, or NULL.
.IP "host_iface" 12
Host interface name, or NULL.
.IP "hostnqn" 12
Host NQN, or NULL.
.IP "hostid" 12
Host Identifier, or NULL.
.IP "out" 12
The allocated TID on success; NULL on error.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Convenience constructor.  NULL fields are stored as NULL.  For an IP
transport (tcp, rdma) a numeric traddr/host_traddr is canonicalized; a
hostname is rejected -- resolving it is the caller's job, not libnvme's.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success (*\fIout\fP is the allocated TID); -EINVAL if \fIout\fP is
NULL or traddr/host_traddr is not numeric on an IP transport; -ENOMEM on
allocation failure.
